  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR RI) is moving forward with the finalization of the Asset Seizure Bill, which concerns assets linked to criminal activities. Following the approval of reports from the internal drafting and synchronization teams, Commission III prepared to hold a plenary meeting for first-level approval. Lawmakers have expressed optimism regarding the legislative timeline, aiming to complete the bill by December 15, 2026. This legislative activity is part of a broader ongoing process within the House to review and process various priority bills before the year ends. Recent discussions have also involved the deliberation of other proposed legislation, including matters related to wiretapping procedures and artificial intelligence regulations, reflecting a period of accelerated legislative focus within the House’s various commissions regarding the national legal framework and prolegnas objectives.",
